# WarpPass worst case: an invisible asteroid parked in front of EVERY
# ship, so each viewport must run its own capture + distortion pass.
# Built for the 1P-vs-4P render-cost measurement (FOURPLAYER.md O6,
# recipe in TESTING.md) rather than for looking at — `sed
# 's/players 4/players 1/'` gives the 1P twin, and dropping the
# `invisible` lines gives a no-lens baseline.
#
# `clear` strips the generated world so the lens pass is what is being
# measured; the one normal asteroid keeps the level-clear countdown from
# rebuilding it mid-run. Ships are 500 apart and their lenses 320 ahead —
# far enough not to collide (a lens overlapping its ship is destroyed on
# contact and the pass then measures nothing, which is how the first
# version of this scene silently reported lens=0).
seed 3
game 6
players 4
clear
camera fixed
ship  0 0
ship2 500 0
ship3 0 500
ship4 500 500
asteroid 0 320 invisible r=120 v=0,0
asteroid 500 320 invisible r=120 v=0,0
asteroid 0 820 invisible r=120 v=0,0
asteroid 500 820 invisible r=120 v=0,0
asteroid 1400 1400 normal v=0,0
sim 20000
